"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f944b8d189ae619d3089f20467fdffd35d6e71afdf8e5c13e7c6d8c18a7845d1","event_uuid":"4ace4880-664c-48fd-8e8f-149801315ae3","position":{"commit_sha":"ca8f43776196037880fe6e2db61c6a04eee51a5e","position":"1787049454528650001-4ace4880-664c-48fd-8e8f-149801315ae3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f9f01e0f3cdfcfdcf1234da270059ab318791b5256da5656efb84e3b8cb94a93","event_uuid":"10cad79d-9cca-4f4f-9eb4-dc30c4ff3c14","position":{"commit_sha":"4f3f058323594fd97c5791d1eb8399cfe8fc5c25","position":"1787049461908921001-10cad79d-9cca-4f4f-9eb4-dc30c4ff3c14"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmed RCA before Phase 2\n\n`close_precheck._completion_precheck` reads ticket state from the relocated tracker correctly, then wrongly derives the code repository as `os.path.dirname(tracker)`. `_referencing_commits` consequently runs `git -C <tracker-parent> log` instead of scanning the explicit/current code checkout. The same root conflation reaches completion-gate config because transition_compute also sets repo_root_str from the tracker parent.\n\nRuntime proof used disposable, separate code and tracker repositories: the correct code-root scan found the trailer commit while the tracker-parent scan returned none. CLI close either emitted the false missing-commit diagnostic when the external parent enabled the gate, or silently closed unsigned when that parent had no gate config. Changing only git -C distinguished the root cause from malformed trailers, resolver failure, reachability, and verifier failure. Default in-repo and true-missing controls remained correct.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. Absolute relocated trackers are documented/supported; the close contract grounds referencing commits in current worktree HEAD.\n\nApproved repair seam: use `config.repo_root(repo_root)` (explicit -> REBAR_ROOT -> cwd Git toplevel), which already resolves the default completion HEAD. Do not use LLM `resolve_code_root`, which may select an attested snapshot and would couple deterministic close logic to the LLM boundary. Normalize both code scan and completion-gate/autoresume config roots; fixing only git -C leaves silent gate bypass.\n\nCaller gate: CLI, library, MCP, and automated import all converge through transition_compute/shared close core; none relies on tracker-parent-as-code. Exact sibling candidate `commit_impact.code_root_for` repeats the tracker-parent assumption for attach-commits and requires separate debugging rather than silent inclusion.","timestamp":1787025631163949001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report.\n\nRoot cause: _completion_precheck correctly read ticket state from a relocated tracker, but conflated the tracker parent with the code repository. It used that wrong root for completion-gate configuration and git commit evidence. Depending on files at the tracker parent, this either falsely rejected a valid referencing commit or silently treated the enabled close gate as disabled and closed unsigned.\n\nRepair: resolve code_root through config.repo_root(repo_root), while continuing to resolve tracker reads independently through config.tracker_dir(repo_root). Use code_root consistently for gate_enabled, referencing/file-impact checks, and completion verifier/autoresume repo_root and cfg_root. This avoids the LLM snapshot resolver because close needs the caller/current code checkout, not an attested material snapshot.\n\nHeld-out proof: tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_custom_tracker_root.py relocates .tickets-tracker outside the repo, enables the gate only in the code repo, creates/starts a ticket through REBAR_TRACKER_DIR, records file impact, creates a real trailer commit in the code repo, and closes through transition_cli. It passed and observed one verifier call, closed state, and certified signature. Exact-defect mutation back to tracker-parent derivation made the oracle fail because the verifier was never called even though the ticket closed; restoration returned GREEN.\n\nRegression sweep: completion-gate suite plus oracle passed 34 tests. The fixer also ran all lifecycle behavior tests (455 passed). make lint and make typecheck pass with the combined worktree.","timestamp":1787026216795956001}],"created_at":1786676746153454001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d64a4c0e-5905-465b-809e-e26dc73afed2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f936-a0b9-e5f8-4def"},{"link_uuid":"9839e267-3819-4e3e-8c3f-5630504a7685","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6dd2-9437-e191-4f08"}],"description":"## Context\nWith an out-of-worktree `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` and a code worktree at a commit carrying the ticket trailer, `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` correctly resolved the trailer but CLI `rebar transition ... closed --ref HEAD` falsely reported that no commit referenced the ticket. `close_precheck.py` derived `code_root = os.path.dirname(tracker)`, so a tracker override made it scan the checkout containing tracker storage instead of the current code worktree. The public library call succeeded when passed the actual repo root, proving the defect and workaround.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a regression test with a code worktree and a separate custom tracker directory.\n- Resolve the code root from the explicit/current repository context while continuing to resolve ticket state from `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`.\n- Preserve the fail-fast no-referencing-commit behavior and default in-repo tracker behavior.\n- Run RED to GREEN, defect-seeded mutation, focused lifecycle tests, gates, and Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] CLI close with an out-of-worktree `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` finds a matching trailer reachable from the current code worktree HEAD.\n- [x] A true missing referencing commit still fails before the completion LLM call.\n- [x] Default in-repo tracker behavior is unchanged.\n- [x] The regression test is RED before the fix and GREEN after reintroducing the correct code-root seam.\n- [x] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, LLM-Review +1, and Verified +1 pass before merge.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"resolve the code repository independently from relocated tracker storage"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_custom_tracker_root.py","reason":"cover CLI close with tracker storage outside the code worktree"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6dd2-9437-e191-4f08"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4ace4880-664c-48fd-8e8f-149801315ae3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["cli","completion-gate","regression"],"ticket_id":"57b6-90b7-87bb-45e7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI close precheck misroots code repo for custom tracker directories","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ebcd8ce9-7fcb-4a28-826e-096c428eea61","3bb43e6d-bdc6-4a68-a87c-38770a94b716","5bef83c9-3751-4f69-a21b-efe023ca3485","81769b8d-e907-48a5-a5a7-8f9da3d02748","e5bf4613-190b-431c-8b92-ade8bed9f023","941694a1-b97c-491d-8029-fd83ceab58e8","9839e267-3819-4e3e-8c3f-5630504a7685","790244b8-e00f-4123-915d-f78f6429474a","1b4588c0-2db6-427d-88f4-f46591c27b45","4ace4880-664c-48fd-8e8f-149801315ae3","10cad79d-9cca-4f4f-9eb4-dc30c4ff3c14"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787052805600946001,"uuid":"f2d515f0-9225-4b9e-bed2-b806e4172d41"}